{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":48.849998474121094,"text":"In 1861, a young and unknown architect won the competition for the most magnificent opera house in the world. Building it took 14 years, and the reason was water. The foundations capped flooding however hard they pumped. In the end, the engineers stopped fighting and did something cleverer. They built an enormous watertight tank and let the water gather in it so that the pressure under the foundations would hold steady. The tank is still there, and the Paris Fire Brigade uses it for dabbing practice. Out of that, and out of an accident with the 7-ton chandelier in 1896, came the story of The Phantom of the Opera, which became a book, and then a film, and a musical, all over the world. The underground lake is real, and you can see photographs of it. The Phantom is not.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.4000000059604645},{"word":"1861","start":0.4000000059604645,"end":1.4600000381469727},{"word":"a","start":1.7400000095367432,"end":1.899999976158142},{"word":"young","start":1.899999976158142,"end":2.180000066757202},{"word":"and","start":2.180000066757202,"end":3.119999885559082},{"word":"unknown","start":3.119999885559082,"end":3.119999885559082},{"word":"architect","start":3.119999885559082,"end":3.5999999046325684},{"word":"won","start":3.5999999046325684,"end":3.9600000381469727},{"word":"the","start":3.9600000381469727,"end":4.380000114440918},{"word":"competition","start":4.380000114440918,"end":4.599999904632568},{"word":"for","start":4.599999904632568,"end":4.960000038146973},{"word":"the","start":4.960000038146973,"end":5.099999904632568},{"word":"most","start":5.099999904632568,"end":5.539999961853027},{"word":"magnificent","start":5.539999961853027,"end":6.119999885559082},{"word":"opera","start":6.119999885559082,"end":6.480000019073486},{"word":"house","start":6.480000019073486,"end":6.699999809265137},{"word":"in","start":6.699999809265137,"end":6.920000076293945},{"wo